From: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 22:30:37 -0400
Subject: Translator: Fix off-by-one error in variable-size check

Bug: chromium:525685715
Bug: chromium:561999377
Change-Id: I67146644ea6da349c5f8208d479e222cbc5eca24
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8414095
Reviewed-by: Yuxin Hu <yuxinhu@google.com>

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y): TParseContext::checkVariableSize on
this ANGLE revision has no mValidatedVariableTypeSizes cache, so only the
comparison change (`>` -> `>=` against kWebGLMaxVariableSizeInBytes) is
applied to the existing code. Test-only hunks that did not apply were
dropped: src/tests/gl_tests/GLSLTest.cpp src/tests/gl_tests/GLSLValidationTest.cpp.

diff --git a/src/compiler/translator/ParseContext.cpp b/src/compiler/translator/ParseContext.cpp
index ce54848c73f7478c192187cc51bfc89c6c849155..a0b4b0040873b71c07869c585ce02ae3a9b43cd9 100644
--- a/src/compiler/translator/ParseContext.cpp
+++ b/src/compiler/translator/ParseContext.cpp
@@ -1823,7 +1823,7 @@ bool TParseContext::checkVariableSize(const TSourceLoc &line,
     const size_t variableSize =
         CalculateVariableSize(type, type->isInterfaceBlock() || type->getQualifier() == EvqUniform)
             .ValueOrDefault(std::numeric_limits<size_t>::max());
-    if (variableSize > kWebGLMaxVariableSizeInBytes)
+    if (variableSize >= kWebGLMaxVariableSizeInBytes)
     {
         error(line, "Size of declared variable exceeds implementation-defined limit", identifier);
         return false;
@@ -1867,7 +1867,7 @@ bool TParseContext::checkVariableSize(const TSourceLoc &line,
         case EvqPerVertexIn:
         case EvqPerVertexOut:
 
-            if (variableSize > kWebGLMaxPrivateVariableSizeInBytes)
+            if (variableSize >= kWebGLMaxPrivateVariableSizeInBytes)
             {
                 error(line,
                       "Size of declared private variable exceeds implementation-defined limit",
